yes(576,'C','An electron moving from a higher to a lower energy level emits a photon with energy equal to the level difference. Hydrogen’s discrete energy levels produce separate spectral lines.',[REB],question='The lines in the hydrogen emission spectrum result from emission of',options=['Electrons from the atom','Energy during proton transitions','Energy during electron transitions','Neutrons from the atom'],audit='Removed unrelated next nuclear-equation question.')
yes(577,'A','Fractional distillation of liquid air separates nitrogen and oxygen because they have different boiling points. The more volatile nitrogen boils off before oxygen.',[REB],question='Which property is used to separate nitrogen and oxygen by industrial fractional distillation of liquid air?',options=['Boiling point','Density','Rate of diffusion','Solubility'],audit='Specified the distillation method already implied by the source industrial separation question; other industrial methods need not use boiling point.')
yes(578,'C','Burning excess phosphorus removes oxygen from the air. Potassium hydroxide absorbs carbon dioxide and other acidic oxides, and concentrated sulfuric acid removes water vapour. Nitrogen and the noble gases remain.',[REB],question='Excess phosphorus is burned in a gas jar of air. The residual gas passes through concentrated KOH solution and then concentrated H₂SO₄. Which gases are collected?',options=['Carbon dioxide, nitrogen and noble gases','Nitrogen dioxide and noble gases','Nitrogen and noble gases','Carbon dioxide, nitrogen dioxide and noble gases'],audit='Made ordinary air-filled gas-jar context explicit; restored oxide names and complete option boundaries.')
