yes(582,'C','Soap lather is a foam: bubbles of gas are dispersed through a liquid film. Thus its dispersed phase is gas and its continuous phase is liquid.',[REB],question='Soap lather is a colloid in which',options=['Liquid is dispersed in gas','Solid is dispersed in liquid','Gas is dispersed in liquid','Liquid is dispersed in liquid'],audit='Corrected leather→lather and old B→C by foam definition; matching Myschool1998 listing also spells lather.')
yes(583,'D','Initial amounts are 0.010 mol HCl and 0.020 mol NaOH. After neutralisation, 0.010 mol OH⁻ remains in 0.200 dm³, so [OH⁻] = 0.050 mol dm⁻³. pOH = 1.30 and pH = 14.00 − 1.30 = 12.70.',[ACID],question='At 25 °C, what is the pH after mixing 100 cm³ of 0.1 mol dm⁻³ HCl with 100 cm³ of 0.2 mol dm⁻³ NaOH, assuming additive volumes?',check='mixed-ph')
